

⭐ CMB SIMULATION DATA FORMAT (Final Form)

This is the single JSON file that sits next to your cinematic output:

run_001.data.json

It contains everything the viewer needs to render overlays, HUD, organisms, and meta‑equation state.

The structure is simple:

{
  "frames": [...],
  "meta": {...}
}

That’s it.

Everything else lives inside those two keys.

⭐ 1. frames[] — Per‑Frame Simulation State

Each frame contains the entire state of the time fabric at that moment.

Each entry corresponds to one video frame.

frames: [
  {
    "t": 0.000,
    "theta": {...},
    "xi": {...},
    "organisms": [...],
    "metric": {...},
    "events": [...]
  },
  ...
]

Let’s break down each part.

🔷 A. "t" — Time

The simulation time for this frame.

"t": 0.0833

Used for:

HUD

Syncing overlays

Blueprint triggers

🔷 B. "theta" — Time Field Θ

This is the core time‑fabric scalar field.

"theta": {
  "min": -0.12,
  "max":  0.87,
  "avg":  0.14,
  "grid": "theta_0001.bin"
}

The "grid" file is optional — if present, the viewer can render:

heatmaps

gradients

curvature

🔷 C. "xi" — Meta‑Model Field Ξ

This determines which time model is active in each region.

"xi": {
  "regime": "WARP",
  "stability": "metastable",
  "transition": false
}

Used for:

regime overlays

blueprint panel

timeline markers

🔷 D. "organisms" — Field Organisms

Each organism is a living structure inside the time fabric.

"organisms": [
  {
    "id": "O1",
    "type": "warp_bubble",
    "stage": "growth",
    "center": [64, 64],
    "radius": 12.4,
    "energy": 0.87
  }
]

Used for:

organism outlines

trails

lifecycle HUD

🔷 E. "metric" — Geometric Field

This describes the local geometry of the simulation.

"metric": {
  "curvature": 0.0031,
  "lightcone": "lc_0001.bin"
}

Used for:

metric grid

curvature map

lightcone overlay

🔷 F. "events" — Blueprint‑Linked Events

These are moments where the blueprint triggers something.

"events": [
  {
    "type": "regime_switch",
    "from": "CLASSICAL",
    "to": "WARP"
  }
]

Used for:

timeline markers

blueprint panel highlights

HUD pulses

⭐ 2. meta{} — Global Metadata

This describes the entire run, not individual frames.

meta: {
  "version": "1.0",
  "resolution": [1280, 720],
  "fps": 60,
  "blueprint": "run_001.cmb",
  "duration": 4.0
}

Used for:

playback sync

viewport scaling

blueprint linking



